## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 (.NET 10)
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, line 94
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch executes per run. If the production code never returns `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate assertion is dead code — a hidden testing gap.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — one execution path is never tested in practice.

---

#### ❷ Sleepy Test — HIGH (downgraded from Critical per integration calibration)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, line 87
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hardcoded 3-second wait introduces non-determinism (too slow on CI, too short under load) and adds 3 seconds to every test run.

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper or `async` wait with timeout:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; the full suite slows linearly with each added sleep.

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, line 113
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion
}
```

**Problem:** The method name implies "no errors," but if `Insert` silently fails (e.g., swallows an exception), this test still passes. It provides false confidence.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** A broken `Insert` path goes undetected — the test always passes.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, line 28
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the failure output is `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` — no indication of *which property* was wrong without opening the source.

**Fix:** Add messages:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned on insert");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage during CI failures — developers must read source to diagnose which property regressed.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✓

The following tests are well-designed:

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, null-check is the assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `3` is contextually obvious (just inserted 3 items) — not Magic Number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate async integration pattern, clear assertion |

The `Setup()` method initializes an **in-memory SQLite** database — this is a hermetic resource, so **Mystery Guest does NOT apply**. The `_connection` and `_repository` fields are used by all tests, so **General Fixture does NOT apply**.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 5 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after bulk insert |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 10 min | Split into two deterministic tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 15 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with async polling helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 5 min | Add message strings to the 4 assertions |

Fixes 1–3 directly prevent **false-pass** scenarios and **flakiness**. Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement for CI triage speed.
